 ================================================================================
                    ADDITIONAL ALGORITHM CLASSIFICATIONS
================================================================================

* NUMBER-THEORETIC ALGORITHM
  Operates specifically on integer properties, divisibility rules, and prime 
  factorization concepts within computational number theory.

* IN-PLACE / CONSTANT SPACE ALGORITHM (O(1) SPACE)
  Executes using a fixed amount of auxiliary memory regardless of input size, 
  storing only a few scalar variables (n, sum, i).

* PSEUDO-POLYNOMIAL TIME ALGORITHM
  Runs in O(sqrt(n)) relative to the numeric value n, but exponential 
  O(2^(b/2)) relative to the bit-length b = log2(n) of the input.

* SEQUENTIAL / SINGLE-THREADED ALGORITHM
  Executes instructions strictly one after another in a single execution thread 
  without parallel processing.

* EXACT ALGORITHM
  Guarantees the precise mathematical answer every time, as opposed to an 
  approximation or probabilistic heuristic algorithm.

